CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     After a successful mmoouunntt, the permissions on the original mount point de‐
     termine if _._. is accessible from the mounted file system.  The minimum
     permissions for the mount point for traversal across the mount point in
     both directions to be possible for all users is 0111 (execute for all).

     Use of the mmoouunntt is preferred over the use of the file system specific
     _m_o_u_n_t__XXXXXX commands.  In particular, mountd(8) gets a SIGHUP signal (that
     causes an update of the export list) only when the file system is mounted
     via mmoouunntt.

BBUUGGSS
     It is possible for a corrupted file system to cause a crash.

